# Cloudflare Pages redirects (https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/).
# Per-project pages live under /projects/<name>/ (item 417). The Projects index keeps a one-line
# summary per project and links out to each page as it lands.
#
# Anchor fragments such as /projects/#server-provisioning are client-side only and never reach the
# server, so a redirect rule cannot match them. They are preserved instead by keeping the matching
# id (id="server-provisioning") on the index summary block, so an old fragment link still scrolls to
# that project's summary, which links on to the full page. The entries below cover PATH-based access
# to the migrated project pages.

/projects/server-provisioning /projects/server-provisioning/ 301
/projects/certificate-secret-renewal /projects/certificate-secret-renewal/ 301
/projects/template-factory /projects/template-factory/ 301
/projects/self-healing-monitoring /projects/self-healing-monitoring/ 301
/projects/decommission /projects/decommission/ 301
/projects/aiops-triage /projects/aiops-triage/ 301
/projects/job-reporting /projects/job-reporting/ 301
/fleet /claude-code/ 301
/fleet/ /claude-code/ 301
